{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.864786Z","id":"ae4a39e318af4253da53e513f3bfb16b141df9f673cf05f29fabd86ad525755e","body":{"detail":"Reverting this canonical(exe) (passing exe as given to upgrade_recently_failed) passes every test. The comparison in replace (line 669) is tested and covers the same case, so this one is either redundant or needs a test of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1203},"end":{"line":1207},"content_hash":"1d92f71c94d077b862e4845a3edce786a4f7884fcc524768cb0baaecc0ecdad0"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test where exe is a symbolic link to a recently failed upgrade's executable and connect_matching must keep the running daemon, or drop the duplicate canonicalization.","summary":"connect_matching's canonical-path comparison has no test","supersedes":"4851131e8d2c710628fe5fe8511199965075fb5c4eb19fab70f410f791864175","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:21:22.865923Z","id":"1b46be8bae4ad27dea967119574d64064d18d3d43953f084ddee9cbf48b43ead","body":{"detail":"They are among the slowest Rust tests on purpose: they show a daemon that never answers is stopped before the rollback, and an old daemon that ignores shutdown is terminated after the grace.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1808},"end":{"line":2034},"content_hash":"0cb758009b591fdd9c767eb9c03c51d3e9ca76cb2d1ee5dabbb39a860853412e"},"summary":"These replacement tests wait out the real 7 s shutdown grace and 5 s readiness deadline","supersedes":"f2ced9e3f2a219b63ffe2a4f5d8a13324c25523bcb0fb68f188f1af6aeb4e3ad","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.713972Z","id":"7bd5309ce6d1aa6e05d2c836558a90e0fb39830ab87d1448358ffe67884b6829","body":{"detail":"SignedClient::send returns a streamed answer unread for any status but 401/429/503 (crates/clax-cli/src/remote.rs:175-178). get_bytes_with then hands a 4xx/5xx answer to Client::finish (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:922), whose res.json() reads the whole body. A remote daemon answering a clip request with a large error body grows the hook's fetch thread without bound until the hook's std::process::exit (at most the hook's deadline, 4 s for the prompt hook), and grows a long-lived caller of get_bytes_with without bound at all.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":979},"end":{"line":1007},"content_hash":"08e433e13c5bc3f7c13ed93c89160fab1c1b7c8a4932a28aa902aa78250e95f0"},"suggested_fix":"Read a non-success streamed answer through the same take(limit) reader (or remote::capped_body) before parsing its error.","summary":"get_bytes_with streams the answer (exec_with(req, true)), so a non-success answer goes to finish, which reads it with res.json() and no size cap; before this change the signed client capped every body at 128 MiB","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/main.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:07:02.775165Z","id":"c93e7e6eed7fe446ce0504e3fbe4f7ba01fa12a09f0c565055dcc80bbc0c2043","body":{"detail":"Spec section 16 lists `clax people` (owner: people, machines and agents), `clax agents` with list and `rename`, and says invites, rights, elevation, narrowing and approval changes print the People link (M20); section 11 names `clax agents rename`. The Cmd enum here has `Agents` and `Approvals` as unit variants (list only) and no People command. docs/contract.md documents `clax agents` and `clax approvals` as listing, and `PUT /api/agents/<handle>` as the rename route (which accepts the owner's token).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":159},"end":{"line":166},"content_hash":"4202bcc21d85b1275cfec7c85f9a1c2ad6ef04e331fa05b293e3a36dc08b3877"},"summary":"Code and spec disagree: there is no `clax people`, `clax agents` has no `rename`, and no CLI command prints the People link for invites, rights, raises, narrowing or approval changes","tags":["task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.101687Z","id":"1aeed14b6215406e53f8abcdcd323c96b2bfa8310431c3f2f7f224ed3f7fa46a","body":{"detail":"Reverting this canonical(exe) (passing exe as given to upgrade_recently_failed) passes every test. The comparison in replace (line 669) is tested and covers the same case, so this one is either redundant or needs a test of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1213},"end":{"line":1217},"content_hash":"6afdf3f37df837abdf81d28698c03335820cc56728965adb1c91a34a7439ea95"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test where exe is a symbolic link to a recently failed upgrade's executable and connect_matching must keep the running daemon, or drop the duplicate canonicalization.","summary":"connect_matching's canonical-path comparison has no test","supersedes":"ae4a39e318af4253da53e513f3bfb16b141df9f673cf05f29fabd86ad525755e","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.103391Z","id":"3cdd6ce548af778e4d8d27ff403121abbbc3162f8bea02a09df0c34450a28702","body":{"detail":"They are among the slowest Rust tests on purpose: they show a daemon that never answers is stopped before the rollback, and an old daemon that ignores shutdown is terminated after the grace.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1818},"end":{"line":2044},"content_hash":"ebab617cfff5bff0dc72a09bc3eaf94bb940c7cfaa529aa81715725036e1338d"},"summary":"These replacement tests wait out the real 7 s shutdown grace and 5 s readiness deadline","supersedes":"1b46be8bae4ad27dea967119574d64064d18d3d43953f084ddee9cbf48b43ead","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:19.104901Z","id":"e7a3616d6a409134cc8c3377700d865f6694bdffa1026406a89e37560b570400","body":{"detail":"SignedClient::send returns a streamed answer unread for any status but 401/429/503 (crates/clax-cli/src/remote.rs:175-178). get_bytes_with then hands a 4xx/5xx answer to Client::finish (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:922), whose res.json() reads the whole body. A remote daemon answering a clip request with a large error body grows the hook's fetch thread without bound until the hook's std::process::exit (at most the hook's deadline, 4 s for the prompt hook), and grows a long-lived caller of get_bytes_with without bound at all.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":989},"end":{"line":1017},"content_hash":"08e433e13c5bc3f7c13ed93c89160fab1c1b7c8a4932a28aa902aa78250e95f0"},"suggested_fix":"Read a non-success streamed answer through the same take(limit) reader (or remote::capped_body) before parsing its error.","summary":"get_bytes_with streams the answer (exec_with(req, true)), so a non-success answer goes to finish, which reads it with res.json() and no size cap; before this change the signed client capped every body at 128 MiB","supersedes":"7bd5309ce6d1aa6e05d2c836558a90e0fb39830ab87d1448358ffe67884b6829","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/main.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:30.047964Z","id":"17fa04509cd60b8855b04b5e8baa70fbe80996fe567aa5cf28724544d5a431ee","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f365ba71","summary":"Fixed: clax people lists people, machines and agents with the People link; clax agents rename renames through PUT /api/agents/<handle> (People link remotely, not_for_agents line under a harness); clax people invite|rights|revoke, clax agents narrow|elevate and clax approvals approve|decide|revoke print the People link, change nothing and exit 2. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-cli --test integration -E 'test(/^people::/) | test(remote_agents_rename)' passes (4 tests); workspace nextest 2256 passed.","supersedes":"c93e7e6eed7fe446ce0504e3fbe4f7ba01fa12a09f0c565055dcc80bbc0c2043","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
